main [main]
  div [notice] role=status
  "Overview"
  div [empty-state]
    "Waiting for your first event"
    "Visitors, pageviews, sessions, and bounce rate for your site, with the top pages, referrers, and devices beside them. Your app sends events with a Rust type for each, so a misspelled property fails when it compiles rather than in a chart. Add leptoskit_analytics with the web and derive features, then send one:"
    div [code]
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "use leptoskit_analytics::Event;"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "use leptoskit_analytics::client::web;"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "#[derive(Event)]"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "struct SignedUp {"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "plan: String,"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "seats: u32,"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "}"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "web::init(web::Options::default());"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "web::capture_event(SignedUp {"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "plan: \"pro\".into(),"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "seats: 3,"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "});"
      button [copy] label="Copy as Rust"
        "Copy"
    "This page lands with the analytics service; until then the admin shows nothing rather than guessing. The guide has the rest: Product analytics."
  "While you wait"
  "Infrastructure already works: plan a change, deploy a release, and read your servers' health."
  a label="Go to Infrastructure" href=/_leptoskit/admin/infra/projects
    "Go to Infrastructure"
